OL,3,GNEWSA'My parents disowned me but Esther
OL,4,ARantzen didn't'
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhen TV presenter Bill Buckley was
OL,7,Fdisowned by his parents after being
OL,8,Fouted as gay by a national newspaper,
OL,9,FDame Esther Rantzen decided to step in,
OL,10,Fwriting them a "beautiful" letter in
OL,11,Fdefence of her colleague.
OL,13,F"She absolutely changed my life... I
OL,14,Fwill be eternally grateful," he said.
OL,15,F"We became great friends and we always
OL,16,Fstayed in touch."
OL,18,FTributes are being paid to Dame Esther,
OL,19,Fwho presented the BBC's That's Life!
OL,20,Ffor 21 years and founded the children's
OL,21,Fcharity Childline, following her death
OL,22,Faged 86.
OL,23,APub: 01-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
